{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The top-level data variables `N_fine_t` and `fine_t` are context inputs used only to configure and compute generated quantities; no data variable is scored by a sampling statement.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. Both parameters have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement in the model block, and the program contains no arbitrary target manipulation or protected-data likelihood to rewrite.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N_fine_t;
  vector[N_fine_t] fine_t;
}

parameters {    
  // Zeroth-order contribution (Baseline)
  real baseline;

  // Logit probability at time zero
  real alpha;
}

model {
  baseline ~ normal(-3, 2);
  alpha ~ normal(4, 2);
}

generated quantities {
  vector[N_fine_t] p = inv_logit(alpha + baseline * fine_t / 365.0);
}

","data_safe_json":"{"N_fine_t":2,"fine_t":[3.0919706408039707,5.70579348244406]}","protected_variables":[]}
